# Article API Backend Conventions

## Service layer

Every `@Service` class must have an interface:

- Interface: `XxxService` in `service/` or `security/`
- Implementation: `XxxServiceImpl` with `@Service`, implements `XxxService`
- Inject the **interface** in components/config, not the implementation

```java
// ✅ GOOD
public interface AuthService { ... }

@Service
public class AuthServiceImpl implements AuthService { ... }

// Component
private final AuthService authService;
```

## HTTP error codes

Use `ErrorCode` enum and typed exceptions extending `ApiException`. REST responses use `ApiErrorResponse` with `code` and `message`.

| Code | HTTP | Use case |
|------|------|----------|
| 200 | OK | Success (GET, PUT) |
| 201 | Created | Register, create article/comment |
| 204 | No Content | Delete |
| 400 | Bad Request | Validation / bad request |
| 401 | Unauthorized | Not logged in / wrong credentials / bad token |
| 403 | Forbidden | Not owner (update/delete article) |
| 404 | Not Found | Resource not found |
| 409 | Conflict | Duplicate username/email |
| 500 | Internal Server Error | Unexpected server error |

### Exception mapping

- `BadRequestException` → 400
- `UnauthorizedException` → 401
- `ForbiddenException` → 403
- `NotFoundException` → 404
- `ConflictException` → 409

### REST error body example

```json
{
  "code": 409,
  "message": "Email đã tồn tại"
}
```

Validation errors (400) may include `errors`:

```json
{
  "code": 400,
  "message": "Validation / bad request",
  "errors": {
    "email": "Email must be valid"
  }
}
```

## Layer structure

- `component/` — MVC controllers + REST controllers
- `service/` — business logic (interface + impl)
- `repo/` — JPA repositories
- `entity/`, `dto/`, `exception/`, `config/`, `security/`
